  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "A hanging side K4^(3) without a line hides the contradiction",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Let H be a connected cubic glue with a switching class without solutions, and a, a' two lines forming a two-vertex cut of its incidence graph, such that that class's restriction to H - a has solutions and the side S meeting a in one point is K4^(3) without a line. Then the class of H - a obtained from the restriction by changing the sign of a' at one of its two points in S has the same row of creation between glue lines, while the restriction ties a's three points and the changed class does not; so one row at a cannot read the tie. Proved from PENDANT-LINE A's locality of creation, a lemma on the side over all 512 signings (one switching class ties its three outer points, every other leaves the two cut points free and the third outer point not a function of them) and six local lemmas on creation's witnesses over all 27 one-point and 3,375 two-point relations; the prediction holds at all 16 failing lines of CONTRA-PROOF's random glues, including the 2 whose hanging side has six points.",
  "dependencies": [
